WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500
Foveated perception for dexterous manipulation.
Watch the robot's actual compact foveated

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:07.000
observation as it grasps the requested object.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.500
Learning robot control directly from perception is
challenging. Simulation can massively scale

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:12.000
learning experience, but high-resolution
perception remains costly. Four GPUs struggle;
eight

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.500
improve learning, yet zero-shot transfer reaches
only 24 percent success in 50 robot trials.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.000
Training curves show time in the success region,
not episode success.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.667
But not every pixel needs equal attention.
Foveation provides detail and context at minimal

00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:24.333
computational cost. The sampling grid and compact
image transform together from uniform to foveated,

00:00:24.333 --> 00:00:28.000
with the same 128 by 128 output size.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.333
Render the foveated view directly. Each output
pixel launches a ray into a standard five-object

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:38.667
clutter scene from the calibrated camera. Rays
reveal the matched native RTX observation.
Rotating

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:44.000
the observation camera changes both the ray bundle
and the RTX image.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.667
Efficient perception enables faster and more
diverse training. A compact observation enables
six

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:49.333
times as many parallel environments and 8.9 times
fewer visual tokens. Full training runs achieve

00:00:49.333 --> 00:00:52.000
4.4 times the throughput.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.500
More GPUs. Consistently higher throughput.
Measured full-run training throughput scales
nearly

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.000
linearly from four to eight L40S GPUs. Foveation
maintains approximately 4.4 times the throughput
of

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.500
uniform high resolution at both budgets. Points
are means of three seeds, with fixed environments

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:58.000
per GPU.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Better training from the same or less compute.
Return to the four- and eight-GPU high-resolution

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.000
curves, then add foveated learning at both
budgets. Foveation also outperforms the matched
low-

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.000
resolution active baseline. Curves show three-seed
mean success-region occupancy over training time.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.333
Zero-shot sim-to-real transfer. Foveated vision
achieves 78 percent success over 50 robot trials,

00:01:14.333 --> 00:01:18.667
versus 26 percent for uniform active and 24
percent for uniform high resolution. Simulation
success

00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:23.000
is 87.6 percent over 2,000 trials.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.000
FOVI-Dex. Foveation enables efficient perceptive
learning of dexterous manipulation in simulation.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.000
Dex Manipulation Workshop, 10th Conference on
Robot Learning (CoRL 2026), Austin TX, USA.
